### Bisa — workflow validation: `problem-<kind>`, the sentence beside a
### `Problem.kind`; a step id or an input name rides as an argument.

## Every problem a definition may have, by kind (crates/bisa-core/src/workflow.rs); a step or input name rides as an argument.

problem-bad-condition-step-all-any-one-condition-needs = step `{ $a0 }`: an all/any/one condition needs at least one condition in `of`
problem-bad-condition-step-conditions-nest-deep-most-allowed = step `{ $a0 }`: conditions nest { $depth } deep; at most { $a1 } is allowed
problem-bad-cron-step = step `{ $a0 }`: { $why }
problem-bad-cron-step-input-should-hold-cron-expression = step `{ $a0 }`: input `{ $input }` should hold a cron expression, got { $a1 }
problem-bad-question-judge-step-asks-confidence-number-from = judge step `{ $a0 }` asks for a confidence of { $c }; it is a number from 0 to 1
problem-bad-question-step = step `{ $a0 }`: { $e }
problem-bad-schema-step-output-schema-not-json-schema = step `{ $a0 }`: its output schema is not a JSON Schema: { $why }
problem-bad-schema-step-schema-not-json-schema = step `{ $a0 }`: its schema is not a JSON Schema: { $why }
problem-bad-template-step-cannot-drive-machine-reads-no = step `{ $a0 }`: {"{"}goal.…{"}"} cannot drive a { $kind_word }; the machine reads no goal
problem-branch-without-rule-flow-out-step-labelled-which-never = a flow out of { $kind_word } step `{ $a0 }` is labelled `{ $b }`, which it never chooses
problem-duplicate-branch-step-chooses-twice = { $kind_word } step `{ $a0 }` chooses `{ $b }` twice
problem-duplicate-branch-switch-step-has-two-cases-value = switch step `{ $a0 }` has two cases for value `{ $a1 }`
problem-duplicate-input-input-declared-twice = input `{ $a0 }` is declared twice
problem-duplicate-step-id-step-declared-twice = step `{ $a0 }` is declared twice
problem-empty-name-step-needs-name = step `{ $a0 }` needs a name
problem-empty-name-workflow-needs-name = the workflow needs a name
problem-empty-rules-decide-step-has-no-rules-so = decide step `{ $a0 }` has no rules, so it would always choose `otherwise`
problem-empty-rules-judge-step-offers-option-s-judgement = judge step `{ $a0 }` offers { $a1 } option(s); a judgement chooses between at least two
problem-empty-rules-switch-step-has-no-cases-so = switch step `{ $a0 }` has no cases, so it would always choose `otherwise`
problem-end-with-successors-end-step-has-flows-out-end = end step `{ $a0 }` has flows out of it; an end ends
problem-input-kind-mismatch-step-input-should-hold-whole-number = step `{ $a0 }`: input `{ $input }` should hold a whole number of seconds, got { $a1 }
problem-input-kind-mismatch-step-reads-input-as-account-but = step `{ $a0 }` reads input `{ $input }` as an account of `{ $connector }`, but it is an account of `{ $wanted }`
problem-input-kind-mismatch-step-reads-input-as-but = step `{ $a0 }` reads input `{ $name }` as { $want }, but it is { $a1 }
problem-labelled-flow-on-plain-step-only-branching-step-decide-if-switch = only a branching step (decide, if, switch, judge, for_each, while) labels its flows, or a boundary event that diverts labels its own; `{ $a0 }` is { $kind_word }, and the label names neither
problem-loop-exit-returns-step-flow-leads-which-flows-back = { $kind_word } step `{ $a0 }`: its `{ $exit }` flow leads to `{ $a1 }`, which flows back into the loop
problem-loop-without-return-step-nothing-side-flows-back-into = { $kind_word } step `{ $a0 }`: nothing on its `{ $body }` side flows back into it, so the loop can never advance
problem-many-starts-step-has-no-incoming-flow-so = step `{ $a0 }` has no incoming flow, and so does another; one step starts
problem-missing-connector-param-step-leaves-unset-which-requires = step `{ $a0 }` leaves `{ $a1 }` unset, which `{ $connector }.{ $operation }` requires
problem-missing-connector-param-step-sets-which-not-parameter = step `{ $a0 }` sets `{ $name }`, which is not a parameter of `{ $connector }.{ $operation }`
problem-needs-goal-step-reads-goal-run-of-workspace = step `{ $a0 }` reads {"{"}goal.statement{"}"} or {"{"}goal.title{"}"}, and a run in the workspace has no goal: read an input instead, or run it on a goal
problem-no-start-workflow-needs-least-one-step = a workflow needs at least one step
problem-no-such-output-step-reads-answer-which-only-human = step `{ $a0 }` reads the answer of `{ $target }`, which is { $kind }; only a human step answers
problem-no-such-output-step-which-human-yields-answer-not = step `{ $a0 }` { $what } `{ $target }`, which is human and yields an answer, not an output; read {"{"}steps.{ $target }.answer{"}"}
problem-no-such-output-step-which-yields-none = step `{ $a0 }` { $what } `{ $target }`, which is { $kind } and yields none
problem-not-assured-step = step `{ $a0 }` { $what } `{ $target }`, { $why }
problem-not-upstream-step-which-does-not-run-before = step `{ $a0 }` { $what } `{ $target }`, which does not run before it
problem-not-upstream-step-which-not-one-check-approval = step `{ $a0 }` { $what } `{ $target }`, which is { $kind } and not one of: check, approval
problem-not-upstream-step-which-not-one-human = step `{ $a0 }` { $what } `{ $target }`, which is { $kind } and not one of: human
problem-notify-author-not-an-agent-step-input-names-who-not-agent = step `{ $a0 }`: input `{ $input }` names `{ $who }`, who is not an agent; only an agent speaks for a workflow
problem-notify-author-not-an-agent-step-speaks-as-who-not-agent = step `{ $a0 }` speaks as `{ $author }`, who is not an agent; only an agent speaks for a workflow
problem-notify-scope-unknown-step-posts-into-which-not-channel = step `{ $a0 }` posts into `{ $scope }`, which is not a channel, a goal or a workstream id
problem-notify-scope-unknown-step-posts-into-which-not-channel-2 = step `{ $a0 }` posts into `{ $rendered }`, which is not a channel, a goal or a workstream id
problem-param-only-placeholder-step-connector-definition-s-step-reads = step `{ $a0 }`: {"{"}params.…{"}"} and {"{"}account.…{"}"} are a connector definition's; a step reads the run
problem-rule-without-flow-step-can-choose-but-no-flow = { $kind_word } step `{ $a0 }` can choose `{ $b }` but no flow carries it
problem-self-flow-step-flows-itself = step `{ $a0 }` flows to itself
problem-self-flow-step-routes-own-failure-itself = step `{ $a0 }` routes its own failure to itself
problem-spawn-cycle-step-spawns-workflow-which-spawns-workflow = step `{ $a0 }` spawns workflow `{ $w }`, which spawns this workflow back; a spawn cycle never finishes
problem-unfilled-input-account-but-which-connector-not = input `{ $a0 }` is an account, but of which connector is not chosen yet
problem-unfilled-step-calls-but-names-no-operation = step `{ $a0 }` calls `{ $connector }` but names no operation yet; pick one
problem-unfilled-step-calls-no-connector-yet-pick = step `{ $a0 }` calls no connector yet; pick one
problem-unfilled-step-checks-no-step-s-output = step `{ $a0 }` checks no step's output yet; pick one
problem-ungated-write-step-calls-which-writes-platform-with = step `{ $a0 }` calls `{ $connector }.{ $operation }`, which writes to the platform, with no `approval` or `human` step before it; add one, or set `unattended: true` to say the write runs on its own
problem-unknown-account-step-input-names-account-which-not = step `{ $a0 }`: input `{ $input }` names account `{ $id }`, which is not an account of `{ $connector }` here
problem-unknown-account-step-input-should-hold-account-id = step `{ $a0 }`: input `{ $input }` should hold an account id, got { $a1 }
problem-unknown-account-step-names-no-account-has-no = step `{ $a0 }` names no account and `{ $connector }` has no default account here; add one under Settings › Capabilities › Connectors, or name one
problem-unknown-account-step-runs-as-account-which-not = step `{ $a0 }` runs as account `{ $id }`, which is not an account of `{ $connector }` here
problem-unknown-assignee-step-names-who-not-workspace = step `{ $a0 }` names `{ $a }`, who is not in this workspace
problem-unknown-connector-step-calls-connector-which-not-installed = step `{ $a0 }` calls connector `{ $connector }`, which is not installed here
problem-unknown-harness-step-names-harness-which-runtime-cannot = step `{ $a0 }` names harness `{ $h }`, which this runtime cannot launch (it has { $a1 })
problem-unknown-input-step-reads-input-which-not-declared = step `{ $a0 }` reads input `{ $name }`, which is not declared
problem-unknown-input-step-tests-input-which-not-declared = step `{ $a0 }` tests input `{ $name }`, which is not declared
problem-unknown-input-step-uses-input-which-not-declared = step `{ $a0 }` uses input `{ $name }`, which is not declared
problem-unknown-model-step-pins-model-which-harness-does = step `{ $a0 }` pins model `{ $m }`, which harness `{ $h }` does not list
problem-unknown-operation-step-calls-which-connector-does-not = step `{ $a0 }` calls `{ $connector }.{ $operation }`, which the connector does not have (it has { $a1 })
problem-unknown-placeholder-step-not-placeholder-platform-knows-write = step `{ $a0 }`: {"{"}{ $key }{"}"} is not a placeholder this platform knows; to write a brace literally, double it ({"{"}{"{"} and {"}"}{"}"})
problem-unknown-project-step-names-project-which-not-workspace = step `{ $a0 }` names project `{ $id }`, which is not in this workspace
problem-unknown-step-step-checks-output-which-does-not = step `{ $a0 }` checks the output of `{ $of }`, which does not exist
problem-unknown-step-step-flows-which-does-not-exist = step `{ $a0 }` flows to `{ $a1 }`, which does not exist
problem-unknown-step-step-names-template-which-does-not = step `{ $a0 }` names `{ $s }` in a template, which does not exist
problem-unknown-step-step-reads-which-does-not-exist = step `{ $a0 }` reads `{ $s }`, which does not exist
problem-unknown-step-step-routes-failure-which-does-not = step `{ $a0 }` routes its failure to `{ $a1 }`, which does not exist
problem-unknown-workflow-step-spawns-workflow-which-not-workspace = step `{ $a0 }` spawns workflow `{ $w }`, which is not in this workspace
problem-unlabelled-flow-on-decide-every-flow-out-step-names-branch = every flow out of { $kind_word } step `{ $a0 }` names a branch
problem-unpromised-output-step-reads-s-output-but-declares = step `{ $a0 }` reads `{ $target }`'s output at `{ $field }`, but `{ $target }` declares no output_schema, so nothing promises `{ $field }`
problem-unpromised-output-step-reads-s-output-step-s = step `{ $a0 }` reads `{ $target }`'s output at `{ $field }`; a { $kind } step's output has only { $a1 }
problem-unpromised-output-step-reads-s-output-which-s = step `{ $a0 }` reads `{ $target }`'s output at `{ $field }`, which `{ $target }`'s output_schema does not require; a result may leave it out — add `{ $field }` to `required`
problem-unreachable-step-cannot-be-reached-from-start = step `{ $a0 }` cannot be reached from the start
problem-unsupported-effort = step `{ $a0 }` pins effort `{ $effort }`, which none of its harnesses can set ({ $harnesses }); name a harness with an effort control, or remove the pin
problem-unused-input-input-declared-but-no-step-reads = input `{ $a0 }` is declared but no step reads it; remove it or reference it as {"{"}inputs.{ $a1 }{"}"}
problem-zero-iterations-step-allows-zero-iterations-least-one = { $kind_word } step `{ $a0 }` allows zero iterations; at least one is needed
problem-zero-visits-step-allows-zero-visits-least-one = step `{ $a0 }` allows zero visits; at least one is needed

## Events and gateways: a start, a wait's catch, an emit and a step's boundary events (crates/bisa-core/src/workflow.rs); a step, an input or an event's name rides as an argument.
problem-bad-poll-file = step `{ $a0 }` polls `{ $connector }.{ $operation }`, which takes the file `{ $param }`; a poll has no file to give
problem-bad-poll-key = step `{ $a0 }` polls without a `key`: name the field, inside one item, that tells one item from another
problem-bad-poll-writes = step `{ $a0 }` polls `{ $connector }.{ $operation }`, which writes to the platform; a start event only reads
problem-bad-signal-name = step `{ $a0 }` names the signal `{ $name }`; a signal's name is dotted lowercase words, like `report.ready`
problem-bad-timer-no-fires = step `{ $a0 }`: the reminder `{ $name }` fires at most zero times; give it a `max` of one or more
problem-bad-timer-schedule = step `{ $a0 }`: a schedule is `every` so many seconds or a `cron` expression — exactly one of the two
problem-bad-timer-schedule-zero = step `{ $a0 }` begins every zero seconds; at least one is needed
problem-bad-timer-zero = step `{ $a0 }`: the boundary event `{ $name }` counts zero seconds; at least one is needed
problem-boundary-on-instant-step = step `{ $a0 }` is { $kind_word } and carries boundary events; only an agent, a human, an approval, a wait or a spawn that waits can be stopped while it is live
problem-duplicate-branch-boundary = step `{ $a0 }` names `{ $name }` twice among its branches and boundary events
problem-manual-start-configured-guard = step `{ $a0 }` begins by hand, so there are no occurrences to guard; remove its `guard`
problem-manual-start-configured-inputs = step `{ $a0 }` begins by hand, so no event fills its inputs; remove its `inputs`, and a person gives the run's inputs when they start it
problem-many-manual-starts = step `{ $a0 }` is one of { $n } starts by hand; a run by hand begins at exactly one
problem-notify-scope-unknown-message-in = step `{ $a0 }` listens in `{ $scope }`, which is not a channel, a goal or a workstream id
problem-reminder-interrupts = step `{ $a0 }`: the reminder `{ $name }` diverts, so it would stop the step at its first tick; let it post or signal beside the step, and divert with a timeout (`after`)
problem-rule-without-flow-divert = step `{ $a0 }`: the boundary event `{ $name }` diverts, but no flow out of the step is labelled `{ $name }`
problem-spawn-needs-manual-entry = step `{ $a0 }` spawns workflow `{ $w }`, which only events start; give it a start by hand, or spawn another
problem-spawn-input-unknown = step `{ $a0 }` gives workflow `{ $w }` an input `{ $name }`, which it does not declare; remove it, or name one it asks for
problem-spawn-input-missing = step `{ $a0 }` spawns workflow `{ $w }`, which requires the input `{ $name }`; say what it is given under the step's inputs
problem-start-has-incoming = step `{ $a0 }` is a start and `{ $from }` leads into it; a start begins a run, and nothing inside one leads back to it
problem-start-placeholder-event-field = step `{ $a0 }`: its event reads `{ $key }`; a start event's fields read the inputs it listens with (inputs.<name>) and nothing else
problem-start-placeholder-event-outside-mapping = step `{ $a0 }` reads `{ $key }`: only a start step's `inputs` read the event — map what you need onto an input there, and read that input here
problem-start-placeholder-mapping = step `{ $a0 }` maps `{ $key }` onto an input; a start's `inputs` read the event (event.<path>) and nothing else
problem-unfilled-project-change = step `{ $a0 }` listens for a project's change but names no project yet; pick one
problem-unfilled-start-polls-no-connector = step `{ $a0 }` polls no connector yet; pick one
problem-unfilled-start-polls-no-operation = step `{ $a0 }` polls `{ $connector }` but names no operation yet; pick a read
problem-unknown-input-start-maps = step `{ $a0 }` maps the event onto `{ $name }`, which is not declared
problem-unknown-topic = step `{ $a0 }` listens for the platform event `{ $topic }`, which this platform never emits
problem-unknown-topic-empty = step `{ $a0 }` listens for a platform event but names no topic
problem-unknown-workflow-run-event = step `{ $a0 }` listens for a run of workflow `{ $w }`, which is not in this workspace

## A connector definition's rules (`Connector::validate`, `ConnectorAccount::validate`), by field.
problem-connector-account-not = the account is for { $a0 }, not { $a1 }
problem-connector-already-header-operation = { $header } is already a header of this operation
problem-connector-base-url-must-be-scheme-host-port = base_url must be scheme://host[:port][/path] with no user info
problem-connector-call-reads-1-pages = a call reads 1 to { $max_pages } pages
problem-connector-client-owns-header-definition-cannot-set = the client owns the { $name } header; a definition cannot set it
problem-connector-client-owns-header-key-travels-platform-s = the client owns the { $header } header; a key travels in the platform's own
problem-connector-clock-s-platform-writes-each-request = `{ $k }` is the clock's; the platform writes it at each request
problem-connector-deadline-1-seconds = a deadline is 1 to { $max_operation_timeout_secs } seconds
problem-connector-declare-least-one-host-connector-may-reach = declare at least one host the connector may reach
problem-connector-definition-bytes-cap = the definition is { $a0 } bytes; the cap is { $max_connector_bytes }
problem-connector-file-parameter-carried-no-part-no-raw = file parameter `{ $a0 }` is carried by no part and no raw body; a file travels only there
problem-connector-header-name-letters-digits-hyphens = a header name is letters, digits and hyphens
problem-connector-host-not-hosts = its host { $a0 } is not in hosts
problem-connector-http-allowed-loopback-host-only-use-https = http is allowed on a loopback host only; use https
problem-connector-key-s-header-query-name-empty = the key's header or query name is empty
problem-connector-multipart-body-needs-least-one-part = a multipart body needs at least one part
problem-connector-must-be-optional-first-page-has-no = `{ $a0 }` must be optional; the first page has no cursor
problem-connector-must-be-text-parameter-cursor-text = `{ $a0 }` must be a text parameter; a cursor is text
problem-connector-needs-parameters-check-runs-with-none = `{ $check }` needs parameters; a check runs with none
problem-connector-next-cursor-dotted-path-with-no-empty = next_cursor is a dotted path with no empty segment
problem-connector-not-field-scheme = { $f } is not a field of the { $a0 } scheme
problem-connector-not-file-parameter-text-part-carries-rest = `{ $file }` is not a file parameter; a text part carries the rest
problem-connector-not-host-write-host-port-suffix = { $h } is not a host: write host[:port] or *.suffix
problem-connector-not-media-type = { $content_type } is not a media type
problem-connector-not-operation-connector = `{ $check }` is not an operation of this connector
problem-connector-not-parameter = `{ $key }` is not a parameter of { $a0 }
problem-connector-not-parameter-operation = `{ $a0 }` is not a parameter of this operation
problem-connector-not-parameter-operation-2 = `{ $file }` is not a parameter of this operation
problem-connector-not-parameter-operation-3 = `{ $from }` is not a parameter of this operation
problem-connector-oauth-url-https-http-loopback-host = an OAuth URL is https:// (or http:// on a loopback host)
problem-connector-only-writing-operation-carries-key-read-safe = only a writing operation carries a key; a read is safe to repeat
problem-connector-operation-declared-twice = operation `{ $a0 }` is declared twice
problem-connector-operation-needs-description = an operation needs a description
problem-connector-output-schema-must-be-json-object = the output schema must be a JSON object
problem-connector-paged-operation-selects-list-pages-output-select = a paged operation selects the list it pages (`output.select`)
problem-connector-parameter-account-parameter-cannot-be-file = parameter `{ $a0 }`: an account parameter cannot be a file
problem-connector-parameter-declared-twice = parameter `{ $a0 }` is declared twice
problem-connector-parameter-needs-label = parameter `{ $name }` needs a label
problem-connector-part-declared-twice = part `{ $a0 }` is declared twice
problem-connector-required = `{ $a0 }` is required
problem-connector-select-dotted-path-with-no-empty-segment = select is a dotted path with no empty segment
problem-connector-signed-token-needs-least-one-claim-iss = a signed token needs at least one claim — an `iss`, an `aud`
problem-connector-signer-s-platform-writes = `{ $k }` is the signer's; the platform writes it
problem-connector-token-lives-1-seconds-default = a token lives 1 to { $max_jwt_ttl_secs } seconds; the default is { $default_jwt_ttl_secs }
problem-connector-write-does-not-page-only-read-followed = a write does not page; only a read is followed across pages
problem-connector-connector-needs-description = a connector needs a description
problem-connector-insecure-tls-loopback-only = an unsigned certificate is accepted on a loopback host only; { $h } is not one
problem-connector-scheme-not-http = scheme { $other } is not http or https
problem-connector-operation-needs-name = an operation needs a name
problem-connector-json-body-object-or-array = a JSON body is an object or array
problem-connector-form-body-needs-field = a form body needs at least one field
problem-connector-form-field-needs-name = a form field needs a name
problem-connector-part-needs-name = a part needs a name
problem-connector-declare-one-operation = declare at least one operation
problem-connector-account-names-no-parameter = {"{"}account.{ $name }{"}"} names no connector parameter
problem-connector-params-account-only = {"{"}params.{ $name }{"}"}: { $field } may read account parameters only
problem-connector-params-names-no-parameter = {"{"}params.{ $name }{"}"} names no parameter of this operation
problem-connector-params-file-in-template = {"{"}params.{ $name }{"}"} is a file; its bytes travel in a multipart part or a raw body, never in a template
problem-connector-reads-params-and-account-only = a definition reads params.<name> and account.<name> only
problem-connector-check-writes = `{ $check }` writes; a check must not
problem-connector-expect-path-dotted = expect.path is a dotted path with no empty segment
problem-connector-expect-equals-or-absent = an expectation says `equals` or `absent`, one of the two
problem-connector-expect-reason-dotted = expect.reason is a dotted path with no empty segment
problem-connector-client-id-param-name = client_id_param is a field name: letters, digits, `_`, `-` and `.`
problem-connector-account-needs-label = an account needs a label
problem-connector-connector-needs-name = a connector needs a name

## An addon manifest's and record's rules (`AddonManifest::validate`, `AddonRecord::validate`), by field (crates/bisa-core/src/addon.rs).
problem-addon-needs-name = an addon needs a name
problem-addon-name-too-long = a name is at most { $max } characters
problem-addon-needs-description = an addon needs a description: it is what a person reads before installing it
problem-addon-description-too-long = a description is at most { $max } characters
problem-addon-version-not-semver = { $version } is not a version: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH, with an optional -pre and +build
problem-addon-license-needed = an addon names its licence
problem-addon-field-too-long = { $field } is at most { $max } characters
problem-addon-url-not-https = { $field } { $url } must start with https://
problem-addon-too-many-tags = { $found } tags; at most { $max }
problem-addon-tag-shape = { $tag } is not a tag: lowercase letters, digits and dashes, at most 32 characters
problem-addon-tag-declared-twice = tag { $tag } is declared twice
problem-addon-window-out-of-bounds = { $field } is { $value } px; a window's edge is { $min } to { $max } px
problem-addon-window-min-above-max = the window's minimum { $axis } is above its maximum
problem-addon-window-size-outside-min-max = the window opens at a { $axis } outside its own minimum and maximum
problem-addon-entry-not-bundle-path = { $entry } is not a path inside the bundle
problem-addon-entry-not-html = { $entry } is not an HTML page
problem-addon-permission-declared-twice = the permission { $word } is declared twice
problem-addon-network-needs-host = a network permission names at least one host
problem-addon-network-host-not-pattern = { $host } is not a host pattern: host[:port], or *.suffix
problem-addon-network-loopback-refused = { $host } is this machine; an addon never reaches the node or anything else on it
problem-addon-grant-not-declared = { $word } was never declared by the addon, so it cannot be granted
